---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/PageIntro.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../../components/CtaBlock.astro';
import WhatsAppButton from '../../components/WhatsAppButton.astro';
import TeamSection from '../../components/TeamSection.astro';
import { WA_MESSAGES } from '../../lib/site';
import { localBusinessSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

const askUs = [
  '"Is this apartment listing real? Is this rent fair?"',
  '"What documents do I need, and which office do I go to?"',
  '"Where do I find a doctor / dentist / pharmacy that speaks English?"',
  '"My landlord says this — is that normal in Cluj?"',
  '"I lost my documents. What do I do, in what order?"',
  '"Where do locals buy this without overpaying?"',
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="For Parents — Someone Local Your Child Can Ask in Cluj"
  description="Your child is moving to Cluj-Napoca. Give them a kind, competent local person to ask about housing, paperwork, and everyday problems — with their consent, on their terms."
  path="/cluj/for-parents/"
  schema={[localBusinessSchema()]}
>
  <Hero kicker="For parents" headline="Someone local, kind, and competent your child can ask in Cluj.">
    <Fragment slot="lead">
      <p>
        Your child is moving to Cluj-Napoca — maybe from another Romanian city, maybe from
        another country. You've done the big things together: the university, the paperwork, the
        packing. What's left is the part no parent can pack for them:
        <strong class="text-ink">the hundred small unknowns of a new city.</strong>
      </p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="cta">
      <WhatsAppButton message={WA_MESSAGES.parent} label="Message us your questions" variant="primary" />
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="reassurance">We're happy to talk with parents — and we'll be just as honest with you as with them.</Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 mt-16 space-y-14">
    <PageIntro title="The problems are usually small. The stress isn't.">
      <p>
        Here's the honest truth about what goes wrong for students in a new city: it's rarely
        dramatic. It's a rental contract they don't fully understand. A deposit that seems high.
        An office that rejected their papers for a reason nobody explained. A weird noise the
        landlord won't fix. A lost ID two days before a trip.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each of these is too small for the university to handle, too local for Google to answer
        well, and too stressful for a young person to carry alone at 9 p.m. in a city they've
        known for three weeks.
      </p>
      <p class="font-medium text-ink">That's the gap we fill.</p>
    </PageIntro>

    <PageIntro title="What your child gets">
      <p>
        A real, local, English-speaking person on WhatsApp — a small team based in the centre of
        Cluj, led by a local PhD, who knows how this city actually works. Before they sign a
        contract, pay a deposit, choose a neighborhood, or stand in a queue, they can ask someone
        who knows what's normal here.
      </p>
      <p>
        While we're new in Cluj, it works simply: they ask a real question, we answer properly,
        and if it helped, we send a payment link with a suggested range — usually a few euros for
        a small question — and they (or you) choose what feels fair. In-person help, like going
        along to an apartment viewing or an office, is by the hour and agreed in advance.
      </p>
    </PageIntro>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 mt-16">
    <PageIntro title="What your child can ask us" />
    <ul class="mt-8 space-y-3">
      {askUs.map((q) => (
        <li class="bg-cream border border-terra-soft rounded-2xl rounded-bl-sm px-4 py-3 text-ink-soft">{q}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-ink-soft">
      And the quieter one behind many messages: <em>"I don't know what to do next."</em> That
      one, we're especially good at.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 mt-16 space-y-14">
    <PageIntro title="How we respect their independence">
      <p>
        We think this matters as much to your child as it does to us, so let's be clear:
        <strong class="text-ink">we work for the student, not as your eyes in Cluj.</strong> Our
        conversations with them are private. We don't send parents reports, and we don't monitor
        anyone. If your child is over 18, the relationship is theirs — you may pay, but they own it.
      </p>
      <p>
        This isn't a limitation. It's the reason it works: students actually use help that
        respects them. What you get isn't surveillance — it's the quiet knowledge that when
        something confusing happens, your child has a competent adult in the city to ask, and
        small problems get handled while they're still small.
      </p>
    </PageIntro>

    <PageIntro title="What we honestly are — and aren't">
      <p>
        We are a local guidance service: practical advice, orientation, recommendations, and
        by-the-hour accompaniment.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are <strong class="text-ink">not</strong> lawyers, doctors, psychologists, police,
        university staff, or immigration officials — and when your child's question needs one of
        those, we say so plainly and help them find the right one. We are
        <strong class="text-ink">not</strong> an emergency service; in any real emergency, 112
        comes first, and everyone we help knows it.
      </p>
      <p>
        We won't promise you we solve everything, because nobody honestly can. We promise your
        child will always have someone local to ask, and will always come away knowing the next
        step.
      </p>
    </PageIntro>

    <PageIntro title="How to set it up">
      <p>
        The best way: <strong class="text-ink">send this page to your child and let them decide.</strong>
        If they want it, the first question takes two minutes to send — and you're welcome to be
        the one who pays what feels fair.
      </p>
      <p>Have questions first? Message us — we're happy to talk to parents.</p>
    </PageIntro>
  </section>

  <TeamSection />

  <CtaBlock
    headline="Give them someone local to ask."
    message={WA_MESSAGES.parent}
    label="Message us your questions"
  >
    <p>
      Many student problems are too small for the university, too local for Google, and too
      stressful to handle alone in a new city. A kind, competent local person changes that.
    </p>
  </CtaBlock>
</BaseLayout>
